cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GeoModel3D, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GeoModel3D: 3D geological models from borehole logs and CPTs, in the browser"
abstract: >-
  Open-source 3D geological and geotechnical modelling in the browser: layered models from borehole logs and cone
  penetration tests (classified by Robertson's soil behaviour type), sections at any angle and along tunnel, road or
  railway alignments, groundwater, stresses, earth pressures, cross-validation of the model, and reports, on real maps in
  the site's national coordinate system.
authors:
  - family-names: Kilic
    given-names: Kursat
    email: kilic_kursat@hotmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/kilickursat/GeoModel3D"
url: "https://kilickursat.github.io/GeoModel3D/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.16.0
date-released: "2026-10-16"
keywords:
  - geological modelling
  - geotechnical engineering
  - borehole logs
  - cone penetration test
  - soil behaviour type
  - stratigraphy
  - cross-section
  - tunnel alignment
  - groundwater
  - WebGPU
